    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to 'total_revenue' and is composed of the three listed line items. 2. 'Total operating cost' is constructed for the oil & gas industry to include all operating expenses before interest and taxes. It includes: Crude oil and product purchases (COGS), Production and manufacturing expenses, Selling, general and administrative expenses, Depreciation and depletion, Exploration expenses, and Non-service pension/postretirement expense. 'Other taxes and duties' (property, excise, etc.) are excluded as they are considered non-income taxes and are part of operating costs; however, they are not listed as a separate line item in the primary statement's 'Costs and other deductions' section for mapping, as they are aggregated into the total. The supplementary note shows they are partially included in Production and SG&A expenses. 3. 'Net income' is mapped to the line attributable to the parent company. 4. 'Taxes' is mapped to 'Income tax expense'. 5. 'Interest expenses' is mapped directly. 6. All values are taken from the primary consolidated statement of income. Numbers in parentheses in the supplementary tables (e.g., net gain on asset sales) are negative but are not used in the primary mapping. 7. The scale is 'millions of dollars' (1E6).",
